{
  "id": "uranium-series-lineage-disequilibrium-environment",
  "name": "Uranium-series lineage disequilibrium in a closed mineral",
  "category": "environment",
  "description": "Closed nuclear-lineage fractions, not conserved mass or released alpha energy. The short-lived Th234/Pa234 intermediates are treated as instantaneous on the1000year output scale; downstream descendants are a cumulative lineage sink, not one physical stable isotope. No chemical transport, recoil loss or inherited daughters. Daughter activities approach secular equilibrium; abundance equality is not equilibrium. Half-lives U2384.468e9yr(rounded),U234245620yr,Th23075584yr; illustrative initial pure-U238 lineage fraction1 with no daughters, horizon1e6yr. Rounded constants and absent inherited daughters preclude precision sample dating. Outputdt1000yr is a numerical choice. Signed net-rate flows encode state equations, not material transport claims. No numerical clipping or arbitrary domain clamps.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.epsl.2013.04.006",
  "reference": "Cheng et al.(2013), Improvements in230Th dating,230Th and234U half-life values, and U-Th isotopic measurements by multi-collector inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry. Bateman(1910) serial-decay equations; primary teaching equations https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/12-744-marine-isotope-chemistry-fall-2012/c9d4092797c06068611c0cfb0903a7d9_MIT12_744F12_Lec4.pdf .",
